Title: 0001-init-uninitialized-members
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: none
Author: aros-micropolis project
Date: 2026-09-15
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: generic - any native platform; hidden in WASM by the zeroed heap

Problem:
  Micropolis reads several members before any assignment:
  setCallback() deletes the old callback value, initMapArrays() allocates
  mapBase/mopBase only under 'if (!ptr)', and clearMap()/setters then
  dereference the results. None of callback, mapBase, mopBase,
  historyInitialized is initialized in the constructor. A freshly
  zeroed WASM heap makes them NULL/false by luck, so the browser build
  never crashed; on AROS (dirty malloc memory) the first calls do:
  observed setCityTax NULL-callback crash, delete-of-garbage in
  setCallback, then writes through poisoned map[] column pointers in
  clearMap().
Solution:
  Initialize all four in the constructor initializer list, in
  declaration order. This is a genuine engine bug on any native
  platform, not an AROS workaround.
Validation:
  Host: ASan build (build/host/harness), 192 phases of haight.cty, clean
  (2026-09-15). Guest: AROS One 1.3 (ABIv11) under QEMU/TCG, GCC 10.5.0,
  192 phases, clean exit, RESULT cityTime=4851 year=2001 month=0.
  Scope: headless
  harness only - no UI, no scenario path, no save.
Removal:
  Permanent fix; candidate for upstreaming to SimHacker/MicropolisCore.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp
index 5230c74..63925da 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp
@@ -86,6 +86,11 @@
  * Simulator constructor.
  */
 Micropolis::Micropolis() :
+        // callback must be initialized: setCallback() deletes the old
+        // value, and init()/setters fire callbacks before any frontend
+        // had a chance to install one. In WASM a fresh zeroed heap hides
+        // this; on AROS (dirty malloc memory) it crashes at once.
+        callback(0),
         populationDensityMap(0),
         trafficDensityMap(0),
         pollutionDensityMap(0),
@@ -101,7 +106,15 @@ Micropolis::Micropolis() :
         fireStationEffectMap(0),
         policeStationMap(0),
         policeStationEffectMap(0),
-        comRateMap(0)
+        comRateMap(0),
+        // mapBase/mopBase are lazily allocated by initMapArrays() under
+        // "if (!ptr)" - an uninitialized value skips the allocation and
+        // poisons every map[]/mop[] column pointer. historyInitialized is
+        // read the same way before any assignment. Same zeroed-heap luck
+        // as callback, same crash on dirty malloc memory.
+        mapBase(0),
+        mopBase(0),
+        historyInitialized(false)
 {
     initMapArrays();
 }
